Subject: [PATCH] Fix Boost.Locale configure with CMake versions that check source_group(TREE)

include/boost/locale.hpp is passed to source_group(TREE include/boost/locale),
but it is next to that folder, not inside it. CMake used to accept this,
because the folder path is a string prefix of the file path. CMake versions
that compare path components stop with "is not a prefix of file".

The file is taken out of the list; it already gets its group on the next line.
---
 libs/locale/CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/locale/CMakeLists.txt b/libs/locale/CMakeLists.txt
index eae5fcf..0e57a05 100644
--- a/libs/locale/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/libs/locale/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -228,6 +228,9 @@ list(FILTER sources_src INCLUDE REGEX "^src/")
 set(sources_inc ${sources})
 list(FILTER sources_inc EXCLUDE REGEX "^src/")
 source_group(TREE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/src/boost/locale" PREFIX "sources" FILES ${sources_src})
+# boost/locale.hpp is next to the TREE folder, not inside it, and gets its group below.
+# CMake versions that check each file against TREE stop with an error on it.
+list(FILTER sources_inc EXCLUDE REGEX "include/boost/locale\\.hpp$")
 source_group(TREE "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include/boost/locale" PREFIX "headers" FILES ${sources_inc})
 source_group("headers" FILES "include/boost/locale.hpp")
 
